        <p>lIAGRA</p>
        <p>Now is the time when the effects of winter's weather on the human system are most noticeable. Scores of people are run-down and ailing, and thus fall easy victims to influenza, colds, chills, rheumatism etc. For t persons who find themselves run-down at this season, ; there is nothing to equal Bile Beans. Read the case of Mr. J. Atherton, a miner, of Ormskirk-road, Pemberton, near Wigan, in proof of their power. He says : "I had got run down and caught a very bad cold. Before I recovered from that, influenza started, and when that left me, I found myself in a truly wretched , condition. I had no appetite, was weak, dizzy when 1 walked, and so troubled with indigestion that I was I afraid to touch food. For days together my head ached' I dreadfully, and I would be absolutely without appetite. I My sight continued to get more and more dim, and the , dizziness to be more troublesome. My whole nervous system seemed to get out of order, and at any sudden sound I would 'jump.' i "My liver became disordered, too, causing me acute pain beneath the shoulders; and constipation was a source of still more ills. I always felt dull, miserable, ' and weak as a child. Then I began to suffer from heart • weakness, and palpitation. This became so bad that at • night I could only sleep on one side. I consulted a doctor, but derived no benefit from his medicine, and , it a as not until I tried Bile Beans that I began to think t I would ever again be well. As I persevered with the , Beans my sight became better, and the feeling of weak- ness left me. Once again I became able to eat and ; enjoy my food, and to digest what I ate. lam now , completely cured, and this I owe to Bile Beans. Such a wonderful medicine should be known everywhere, and shall always recommend it." ; Bile Beans are the finest known remedy for liver and kidney ailments, indigestion, debility, colds, chill, rheumatism, influenza constipation, piles, loss of appetite, nausea, headache, and all female ailments. I Obtainable from all chemists at is. lid. or 2s. 9d. per I ; box.</p>
